<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">How many lights does a Christmas tree need? The usual rule is about 100 lights per foot of tree height, so a 7 ft tree needs around 700 lights, and 150 or even 200 per foot if you like a fuller, brighter look. This <strong>Christmas tree lights calculator</strong> works it out for your tree in two taps, and tells you how many strands to buy.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Pick your tree height and the look you want. You also get a full shopping list: how many ornaments, how much garland and how much ribbon. Open <em>More options</em> for a slim or pencil tree, a different strand size or an exact height in feet or centimetres.</p>



<div id="dsh-xl" class="dsh-calc">

