<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Christmas Tree Lights FAQ</h2>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How many lights do I need for a 7 ft Christmas tree?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A 7 ft tree needs about 700 lights for a classic look, using the rule of 100 lights per foot. For a fuller look use about 1,050 lights (150 per foot), and for an extra bright tree about 1,400 (200 per foot). That is 7, 11 or 14 strands of 100.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How many lights do I need for a 6 ft Christmas tree?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Plan about 600 lights for a 6 ft tree, or 900 for a fuller look. With 100-light strands that is 6 or 9 sets. A slim 6 ft tree needs fewer, around 420 for the classic look, because it has less branch surface.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How many lights for a 7.5 ft tree?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A 7.5 ft tree needs about 750 lights for the classic 100-per-foot look, about 1,130 for a full look and about 1,500 for extra bright. If your tree is pre-lit, check how many lights it already has before you buy more.</p>



<h3 class="wp-block-heading">How many ornaments and how much garland do I need?</h3>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">For a 7 ft tree, plan 70 to 105 standard ornaments (10 to 15 per foot), about 63 ft (19 m) of garland and at least 21 yards (19 m) of ribbon. The calculator above works these out for any tree height.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">More Holiday Guides</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">When the season is over, our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/christmas-decoration-storage/">Christmas decoration storage ideas</a> help you pack the lights so they do not tangle. Setting the table? See our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/christmas-table-decoration-ideas/">Christmas table decoration ideas</a>, and for wrapping, our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/gift-wrap-storage-ideas/">gift wrap storage ideas</a>. Planning the room around the tree? Try our <a href="https://dailyspacehacks.com/rug-size-calculator/">rug size calculator</a>.</p>



